Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:51:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] bscdeps: machine-readable dependency discovery (plan P1)

The discovery interface delivery-plan phase P1 requires: report the
package closure that bsc -u would walk -- post-preprocessing imports,
search-path resolution under the effective flags, includes, modules to
elaborate, foreign imports -- as tab-separated lines an external
coordinator consumes, plus the negative probes (candidate paths that lost
to each resolution) so a coordinator can depend on their continued
absence and re-resolve when a newly shadowing file appears (the P1 exit
test).

Implemented as a thin executable client over the compiler's own Depend
module, per the plan's "compiler mode using the same modules; do not
duplicate the parser or scrape human diagnostics": Depend additionally
exports findPackages, PkgInfo and CompileStatus (an additive export-list
change only). The probe lists mirror FileIOUtil's candidate order
(file-major over the search path, sources before the binary fallback);
the mirroring is commented at both constructions.

Gate: cabal build bsc:exe:bscdeps, then compare its graph against a
bluetcl makedepend run over src/Libraries; no toolchain in this
container.

